       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Amlodipine 20 mg once daily is double the FDA-labeled maximum of 10 mg per day. A 70 kg adult with normal kidney and liver function doesn't have a factor that would justify the higher dose. Doses above 10 mg mostly add peripheral edema, hypotension, and reflex tachycardia, with little extra blood pressure benefit.\n\nYou could do one of these:\n1. **Enter 10 mg PO once daily**, the maximum standard dose.\n2. **Enter 5 mg PO once daily**, the usual starting dose, and titrate up.\n3. **Keep 20 mg PO once daily**, if you intend it. Tell me and I'll enter it with a note that the dose was confirmed as intentional.\n\nIf blood pressure is still uncontrolled on 10 mg, adding a second agent such as an ACE inhibitor, an ARB, or a thiazide-type diuretic is usually preferred to going higher on amlodipine.\n\nWhich option do you want?"
      }
     ],
